license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. Let H be the subgroup of order three of a Singer cycle group of PG(2,13), which fixes no point. Every H-invariant blocking set of PG(2,13) meets some line in at least five points, and the 21-point blocking set of Blokhuis, Brouwer and Wilbrink attains five, so five is the least possible largest line intersection of an H-invariant blocking set. This settles one symmetric case of Erdos Problem 1159 for the plane of order 13. A Lean 4 proof, including a kernel-checked exhaustive search, and an independent exact checker are included. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
